NOTE: 

streamfunction1 is for drag1
streamfunction2 is for drag2

The examples in this directory are described in the userguide.

Short description
-----------------

drag1

 2D Stokes problem on a square domain with a single particle.
 Boundary fitted mesh.
 Set forces/torque to 1 to find the inverse drag coefficients.

fh1

 2D Stokes problem on a square domain with a single particle.
 Brownian forces using fluctuating hydrodynamics.
 Boundary fitted mesh.
 No movement of the particle in order to estimate the diffusion coefficient
 from the sample and check the Stokes-Einstein-Sutherland relation.

drag2

 2D Stokes problem on a square domain with a single particle.
 Fictitious domain method with a rigid-ring description.
 Weak Lagrange multiplier implementation.
 Set forces/torque to 1 to find the inverse drag coefficients.

fh2

 2D Stokes problem on a square domain with a single particle.
 Brownian forces using fluctuating hydrodynamics.
 Weak Lagrange multiplier implementation.
 No movement of the particle in order to estimate the diffusion coefficient
 from the sample and check the Stokes-Einstein-Sutherland relation.

fh3

 Fluctuating Stokes problem:
 Circle confined in a rectangular domain under the effect of an external
 harmonic potential.
 Predictor-Corrector time integration scheme to account for the divergence
 of the mobility.
 ALE body-fitting mesh scheme.
 Mesh generated by Gmsh using triangles.
 A remeshing is performed when the maximum normalized area or aspect ratio 
 of the mesh elements is higher than a threshold.

